-- safe.l4 — the instrument, one Safe, section by section.
--
-- Source form: Y Combinator, "Postmoney Safe — Valuation Cap Only", version 1.2, with the
-- Discount Only and MFN Only forms where they differ (variation register, axis A).
-- © 2023 Y Combinator Management, LLC, CC BY-ND 4.0 International. Every quotation below
-- is from those forms; section labels are the forms' own.
--
-- Division of labour: this module states what ONE Safe is entitled to, given the
-- capitalisation figures the definitions in §2 call for. Computing those figures for a
-- whole cap table — the Company Capitalization fixpoint, the round price, who converts
-- and who cashes out — is safe-portfolio.l4's job, and it hands the results in here.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `safe-form`

§ `Terms`

-- The three published economic variants, as one type (SPEC.md ruling R3).
DECLARE EconomicTerms IS ONE OF
    `Valuation Cap`       HAS `Post-Money Valuation Cap` IS A NUMBER
    `Discount`            HAS `Discount Rate`            IS A NUMBER   -- as printed: "[100 minus the discount]%"
    `Most Favored Nation`

GIVEN safe IS A SafeIn
GIVETH AN EconomicTerms
`terms of` safe MEANS
    CONSIDER safe's terms's cap
    WHEN JUST c  THEN `Valuation Cap` c
    WHEN NOTHING THEN CONSIDER safe's terms's discount
                      WHEN JUST d  THEN `Discount` (100 MINUS d)
                      WHEN NOTHING THEN `Most Favored Nation`

GIVEN safe IS A SafeIn
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- "in exchange for the payment by [Investor Name] (the “Investor”) of $[_____] (the
-- “Purchase Amount”)"
`Purchase Amount` safe MEANS safe's purchaseAmount

§ `1. Events`

§§ `(a) Equity Financing`

-- The figures §1(a) needs, as of the initial closing. The first is the round's; the
-- second is the §2 definition, computed for the whole cap table by safe-portfolio.l4.
DECLARE `Equity Financing` HAS
    `lowest price per share of the Standard Preferred Stock` IS A NUMBER
    `Company Capitalization`                                 IS A NUMBER

-- "If there is an Equity Financing before the termination of this Safe, on the initial
-- closing of such Equity Financing, this Safe will automatically convert into the greater
-- of: (1) the number of shares of Standard Preferred Stock equal to the Purchase Amount
-- divided by the lowest price per share of the Standard Preferred Stock; or (2) the
-- number of shares of Safe Preferred Stock equal to the Purchase Amount divided by the
-- Safe Price."                                                        — cap form
-- "… will automatically convert into the number of shares of Safe Preferred Stock equal
-- to the Purchase Amount divided by the Discount Price."              — discount form
-- "… will automatically convert into the number of shares of Standard Preferred Stock
-- equal to the Purchase Amount divided by the lowest price per share of the Standard
-- Preferred Stock."                                                   — MFN form
GIVEN safe IS A SafeIn
      financing IS AN `Equity Financing`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`shares on conversion` safe financing MEANS
    CONSIDER `terms of` safe
    WHEN `Valuation Cap` cap THEN
        max (`Purchase Amount` safe DIVIDED BY lowest)
            (`Purchase Amount` safe DIVIDED BY `Safe Price` cap (financing's `Company Capitalization`))
    WHEN `Discount` rate THEN
        `Purchase Amount` safe DIVIDED BY `Discount Price` lowest rate
    WHEN `Most Favored Nation` THEN
        `Purchase Amount` safe DIVIDED BY lowest
  WHERE
    lowest MEANS financing's `lowest price per share of the Standard Preferred Stock`

-- Which class the shares are: Safe Preferred Stock when the Safe Price or the Discount
-- Price governs, Standard Preferred Stock otherwise. The cap form's "greater of" resolves
-- to (2) exactly when the Safe Price is below the round price.
GIVEN safe IS A SafeIn
      financing IS AN `Equity Financing`
GIVETH A STRING
`class on conversion` safe financing MEANS
    CONSIDER `terms of` safe
    WHEN `Valuation Cap` cap THEN
        IF `Safe Price` cap (financing's `Company Capitalization`) LESS THAN financing's `lowest price per share of the Standard Preferred Stock`
        THEN "Safe Preferred Stock"
        ELSE "Standard Preferred Stock"
    WHEN `Discount` rate THEN "Safe Preferred Stock"
    WHEN `Most Favored Nation` THEN "Standard Preferred Stock"

§§ `(b) Liquidity Event`

-- The figures §1(b) needs, as of immediately prior to the Liquidity Event.
DECLARE `Liquidity Event` HAS
    `Proceeds`                               IS A NUMBER   -- "cash and other assets … legally available for distribution"
    `Liquidity Capitalization`               IS A NUMBER   -- §2, computed by safe-portfolio.l4
    `fair market value of the Common Stock`  IS A NUMBER   -- the discount and MFN forms' Liquidity Price basis
    `indebtedness and creditor claims`       IS A NUMBER   -- §1(d)(i): paid first

-- "the Investor will automatically be entitled … to receive a portion of Proceeds …
-- equal to the greater of (i) the Purchase Amount (the “Cash-Out Amount”) or (ii) the
-- amount payable on the number of shares of Common Stock equal to the Purchase Amount
-- divided by the Liquidity Price (the “Conversion Amount”)."          — cap and discount forms
-- "… equal to the Purchase Amount (the “Cash-Out Amount”)."           — MFN form
GIVEN safe IS A SafeIn
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Cash-Out Amount` safe MEANS `Purchase Amount` safe

GIVEN safe IS A SafeIn
      event IS A `Liquidity Event`
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- the number of shares of Common Stock the Conversion Amount is measured on
`Conversion Amount shares` safe event MEANS
    `Purchase Amount` safe DIVIDED BY `Liquidity Price` safe event

GIVEN safe IS A SafeIn
      event IS A `Liquidity Event`
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- "the amount payable on" those shares: their share of the Proceeds, on an as-converted
-- basis, which is Proceeds ÷ Liquidity Capitalization per share (User Guide p. 21).
`amount payable on the Conversion Amount` safe event MEANS
    `Conversion Amount shares` safe event TIMES (event's `Proceeds` DIVIDED BY event's `Liquidity Capitalization`)

GIVEN safe IS A SafeIn
      event IS A `Liquidity Event`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`liquidity entitlement` safe event MEANS
    CONSIDER `terms of` safe
    WHEN `Most Favored Nation` THEN `Cash-Out Amount` safe
    OTHERWISE max (`Cash-Out Amount` safe) (`amount payable on the Conversion Amount` safe event)

GIVEN safe IS A SafeIn
      event IS A `Liquidity Event`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Whether this Safe takes the Conversion Amount rather than cashing out. §2's Liquidity
-- Capitalization excludes "Safes … where the holders … are receiving Cash-Out Amounts",
-- so safe-portfolio.l4 needs this to compute the figure it hands back in.
DECIDE `takes the Conversion Amount` safe event IF
        (NOT (`terms of` safe EQUALS `Most Favored Nation`))
    AND `amount payable on the Conversion Amount` safe event GREATER THAN `Cash-Out Amount` safe

§§ `(c) Dissolution Event`

-- "If there is a Dissolution Event before the termination of this Safe, the Investor
-- will automatically be entitled (subject to the liquidation priority set forth in
-- Section 1(d) below) to receive a portion of Proceeds equal to the Cash-Out Amount"
GIVEN safe IS A SafeIn
GIVETH A NUMBER
`dissolution entitlement` safe MEANS `Cash-Out Amount` safe

§§ `(d) Liquidation Priority`

-- "The Investor’s right to receive its Cash-Out Amount is: (i) Junior to payment of
-- outstanding indebtedness and creditor claims …; (ii) On par with payments for other
-- Safes and/or Preferred Stock, and if the applicable Proceeds are insufficient to permit
-- full payments to the Investor and such other Safes and/or Preferred Stock, the
-- applicable Proceeds will be distributed pro rata to the Investor and such other Safes
-- and/or Preferred Stock in proportion to the full payments that would otherwise be due;
-- and (iii) Senior to payments for Common Stock."
--
-- What one Safe actually receives of its Cash-Out Amount, given the Proceeds, the senior
-- claims and the total of all pari passu cash-out claims. Preferred Stock preferences
-- rank with the Safes here and are folded into `pari passu claims` by the caller.
GIVEN safe IS A SafeIn
      proceeds IS A NUMBER
      `senior claims` IS A NUMBER
      `pari passu claims` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cash-out actually paid` safe proceeds `senior claims` `pari passu claims` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF available AT MOST 0 THEN 0
        IF available AT LEAST `pari passu claims` THEN `Cash-Out Amount` safe
        OTHERWISE `Cash-Out Amount` safe TIMES available DIVIDED BY `pari passu claims`
  WHERE
    available MEANS proceeds MINUS `senior claims`

§§ `(e) Termination`

-- "This Safe will automatically terminate … immediately following the earliest to occur
-- of: (i) the issuance of Capital Stock to the Investor pursuant to the automatic
-- conversion of this Safe under Section 1(a); or (ii) the payment, or setting aside for
-- payment, of amounts due the Investor pursuant to Section 1(b) or Section 1(c)."
DECLARE History HAS
    `Capital Stock has been issued on conversion`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `amounts due under 1(b) or 1(c) have been paid or set aside` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN history IS A History
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Safe has terminated` history IF
        history's `Capital Stock has been issued on conversion`
    OR  history's `amounts due under 1(b) or 1(c) have been paid or set aside`

§ `2. Definitions`

GIVEN cap IS A NUMBER
      `Company Capitalization` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- "“Safe Price” means the price per share equal to the Post-Money Valuation Cap divided
-- by the Company Capitalization."
`Safe Price` cap `Company Capitalization` MEANS cap DIVIDED BY `Company Capitalization`

GIVEN `lowest price per share of the Standard Preferred Stock` IS A NUMBER
      `Discount Rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- "“Discount Price” means the lowest price per share of the Standard Preferred Stock sold
-- in the Equity Financing multiplied by the Discount Rate."           — discount form
`Discount Price` `lowest price per share of the Standard Preferred Stock` `Discount Rate` MEANS
    `lowest price per share of the Standard Preferred Stock` TIMES `Discount Rate` DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN safe IS A SafeIn
      event IS A `Liquidity Event`
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- "“Liquidity Price” means the price per share equal to the Post-Money Valuation Cap
-- divided by the Liquidity Capitalization."                           — cap form
-- "… the fair market value of the Common Stock at the time of the Liquidity Event, as
-- determined by reference to the purchase price payable in connection with such Liquidity
-- Event, multiplied by the Discount Rate."                            — discount form
-- "… the fair market value of the Common Stock at the time of the applicable Liquidity
-- Event (determined by reference to the purchase price payable in connection with such
-- Liquidity Event)."  — MFN form, where it is used only by Dividend Amount (register E4)
`Liquidity Price` safe event MEANS
    CONSIDER `terms of` safe
    WHEN `Valuation Cap` cap THEN cap DIVIDED BY event's `Liquidity Capitalization`
    WHEN `Discount` rate THEN event's `fair market value of the Common Stock` TIMES rate DIVIDED BY 100
    WHEN `Most Favored Nation` THEN event's `fair market value of the Common Stock`

GIVEN safe IS A SafeIn
      event IS A `Liquidity Event`
      `dividend per share of Common Stock` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- "“Dividend Amount” means, with respect to any date on which the Company pays a dividend
-- on its outstanding Common Stock, the amount of such dividend that is paid per share of
-- Common Stock multiplied by (x) the Purchase Amount divided by (y) the Liquidity Price
-- (treating the dividend date as a Liquidity Event solely for purposes of calculating
-- such Liquidity Price)."
`Dividend Amount` safe event `dividend per share of Common Stock` MEANS
    `dividend per share of Common Stock` TIMES (`Purchase Amount` safe DIVIDED BY `Liquidity Price` safe event)

§ `5. Miscellaneous`

§§ `(a) Amendment by a majority-in-interest`

-- "Any provision of this Safe may be amended, waived or modified by written consent of the
-- Company and either (i) the Investor or (ii) the majority-in-interest of all
-- then-outstanding Safes with the same “Post-Money Valuation Cap” and “Discount Rate” as
-- this Safe (and Safes lacking one or both of such terms will be considered to be the same
-- with respect to such term(s)) … “Majority-in-interest” refers to the holders of the
-- applicable group of Safes whose Safes have a total Purchase Amount greater than 50% of
-- the total Purchase Amount of all of such applicable group of Safes."
GIVEN a IS A SafeIn
      b IS A SafeIn
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `same terms group` a b IF
        a's terms's cap EQUALS b's terms's cap
    AND a's terms's discount EQUALS b's terms's discount

GIVEN safe IS A SafeIn
      outstanding IS A LIST OF SafeIn
      consenting IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- TRUE when the consenting holders form a majority-in-interest of this Safe's group.
DECIDE `majority-in-interest consents` safe outstanding consenting IF
    consentingAmount GREATER THAN groupAmount DIVIDED BY 2
  WHERE
    group MEANS filter (GIVEN s YIELD `same terms group` safe s) outstanding
    groupAmount MEANS sum (map (GIVEN s YIELD s's purchaseAmount) group)
    consentingAmount MEANS sum (map (GIVEN s YIELD s's purchaseAmount) (filter (GIVEN s YIELD elem (s's investor's name) consenting) group))

§ `3. “MFN” Amendment Provision (MFN form only)`

-- "If the Company issues any Subsequent Convertible Securities with terms more favorable
-- than those of this Safe (including, without limitation, a valuation cap and/or discount)
-- prior to termination of this Safe, the Company will promptly provide the Investor with
-- written notice thereof, together with a copy of such Subsequent Convertible Securities
-- (the “MFN Notice”) … In the event the Investor determines that the terms of the
-- Subsequent Convertible Securities are preferable to the terms of this instrument, the
-- Investor will notify the Company in writing within 10 days of the receipt of the MFN
-- Notice. Promptly after receipt of such written notice from the Investor, the Company
-- agrees to amend and restate this instrument to be identical to the instrument(s)
-- evidencing the Subsequent Convertible Securities."                   — MFN form, §3
--
-- The family's one hard deadline (10 days) and two soft ones ("promptly", supplied as a
-- number of days by the caller). The Investor's step is a permission: not electing
-- discharges the provision; the Company's failure at either end is a breach.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Company
    Investor

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    `provide the MFN Notice`
    `notify the Company that the terms are preferable`
    `amend and restate this Safe to be identical`

GIVEN promptly IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`MFN Amendment Provision` promptly MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `provide the MFN Notice`
    WITHIN promptly
    HENCE PARTY Investor
          MAY `notify the Company that the terms are preferable`
          WITHIN 10
          HENCE PARTY Company
                MUST `amend and restate this Safe to be identical`
                WITHIN promptly
                LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the Company did not amend and restate the Safe after the Investor's MFN election"
          LEST FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the Company issued more favorable Subsequent Convertible Securities without giving the MFN Notice"
